## Interim recipe manifest

Path: `<catalog>/<dir>/recipes/agents.yaml`

```yaml
defaults:
  resources: remote-llm
  kits: []
agents:
  cursor:
    sbx_agent: cursor
    kits: []
    image_name: ""   # optional custom template
```

Formal spec is still evolving (`sbx-kit experimental spec`). Do not invent `spec.yaml`; kit schema belongs to sbx.

## Upstream sbx docs (read when needed)

Use these for sbx-native concepts — sbx-kit intentionally delegates here instead of copying specs:

| Topic | Link | When an agent needs it |
|-------|------|-------------------------|
| Sandboxes overview | https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/ | Isolation, `sbx run`, daemon, what runs inside the box |
| Customize | https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/ | **Templates vs kits** — image bake vs YAML at create |
| Integrations | https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/integrations/ | SSH `.sbx`, workspace mount paths, Cursor remote |
| Kit spec v2 | https://github.com/docker/sbx-kits-contrib/blob/main/spec/SPEC-v2.md | Authoring or migrating `kits/*/spec.yaml` (`agentContext` / `agentInstructions`) |

Do not implement kit schema or v1→v2 migration in sbx-kit — use sbx CLI and the spec above.

## Host vs box

- **Host**: catalog path, git directories, secrets, bindings, state archives, `sbx-kit` commands, **this skill**
- **Box**: agent session, overlay under `/etc/sbx-kit/`, `/home/agent`, `sbx exec` — see overlay `context.md` then Docker Sandboxes docs

## box check vs recipes verify

- `sbx-kit box check` — bound sandbox + recipe kits + `sbx secret ls` (runtime readiness)
- `sbx-kit recipes verify` — catalog content before create (manifest + delegated kit validate)

